<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>World news and headlines - RFI</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events in France, Europe and around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 17:41:24 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>International</category><title>France, Germany, UK condemn Iran attacks as renewed fighting with US puts peace deal at risk</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260713-france-germany-uk-condemn-iran-attacks-as-renewed-fighting-with-us-puts-peace-deal-at-risk</link><description>
The foreign ministers of France, Germany, and Britain have condemned Iran's attacks on shipping in the Strait of Hormuz and on countries in the region, as Iran and the United States have traded attacks in recent days, casting doubt on their interim agreement to end the war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3ec205ec-7ea5-11f1-bf7e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T053825Z-34279053-RC2ORKA8YMAI-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-JET-FUEL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3ec205ec-7ea5-11f1-bf7e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T053825Z-34279053-RC2ORKA8YMAI-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-JET-FUEL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">44770c08-7ec8-11f1-a564-dbb701fa6098</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 15:47:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3ec205ec-7ea5-11f1-bf7e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T053825Z-34279053-RC2ORKA8YMAI-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-JET-FUEL.jpg">© Retuers</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Ukraine's allies gather in Paris as Kremlin dismisses 'coalition of warmongers'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260713-ukraine-s-allies-gather-in-paris-as-kremlin-dismisses-coalition-of-warmongers</link><description>
Allies of Ukraine gathered in Paris on Monday alongside President Volodymyr Zelensky to reaffirm their support for Kyiv and step up pressure on Russia, at a summit of the so-called "Coalition of the Willing" that the Kremlin promptly dismissed as a meeting of leaders who "do not want peace".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c048ec60-7e88-11f1-b680-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-98RE6CT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c048ec60-7e88-11f1-b680-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-98RE6CT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">48600820-7e95-11f1-94fb-79dafa8f9333</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 14:46:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c048ec60-7e88-11f1-b680-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-98RE6CT.jpg">AFP - HANDOUT</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France to summon Russian ambassador over cyber attacks</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260713-france-to-summon-russian-ambassador-over-cyber-attacks-as-eu-imposes-sanctions</link><description>
France will summon the Russian ambassador to Paris over an alleged Russian cyberhacking campaign against European countries including France, as the EU and Britain targeted Russia with coordinated sanctions. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7e478ee8-7ea1-11f1-824b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T082209Z-700640867-RC2M3LAVNOCA-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-RUSSIA-FRANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7e478ee8-7ea1-11f1-824b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T082209Z-700640867-RC2M3LAVNOCA-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-RUSSIA-FRANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fa43c21a-7ea0-11f1-9bd8-d560f093ee90</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 14:06:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7e478ee8-7ea1-11f1-824b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T082209Z-700640867-RC2M3LAVNOCA-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-RUSSIA-FRANCE.jpg">© Alice Sacco/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Trump lifts Turkey sanctions, eyes F-35 sale</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260713-trump-lifts-turkey-sanctions-eyes-f-35-sale</link><description>
US President Donald Trump made headlines this week at the Nato summit in Ankara by declaring an end to all sanctions against Turkey, paving the way for the sale of the F-35 stealth fighter jet to the alarm of Greece and Israel.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/13d2c946-7ea2-11f1-832c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08t165506z-1517548943-rc2s9magdwgg-rtrmadp-3-nato-summit-trump.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/13d2c946-7ea2-11f1-832c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08t165506z-1517548943-rc2s9magdwgg-rtrmadp-3-nato-summit-trump.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0d2c9f5c-7ea4-11f1-a02f-d560f093ee90</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 10:19:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dorian Jones</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Record 128 migrants cross Channel in one boat as overall numbers drop</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260713-record-128-migrants-cross-channel-in-one-boat-even-as-overall-numbers-drop</link><description>
A small boat carrying 128 people has reached the coast of England, marking a new record for the largest single crossing of the Channel on a small boat, even as the number of crossings has dropped in recent months.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e6ad9c5e-5e51-11f1-b870-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-23T112320Z-1587055107-RC2TELAIYLCQ-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-MIGRATION-FRANCE-BRITAIN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e6ad9c5e-5e51-11f1-b870-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-23T112320Z-1587055107-RC2TELAIYLCQ-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-MIGRATION-FRANCE-BRITAIN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4676965a-7e9a-11f1-b6e4-efef7f7c984b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 09:57:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e6ad9c5e-5e51-11f1-b870-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-23T112320Z-1587055107-RC2TELAIYLCQ-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-MIGRATION-FRANCE-BRITAIN.jpg">© Dylan Martinez/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>China's missile test overshadowed by Iran war, but Pacific nations are watching</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260713-china-s-missile-test-overshadowed-by-iran-war-but-pacific-nations-are-watching</link><description>
China recenly test-fired a nuclear-capable missile from a submarine into the Pacific, the first such launch from a nuclear-powered vessel and the first submarine-based test since 1982.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9974988c-7b9a-11f1-9a4c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Jin-Type-094-Class-Ballistic-Missile-Submarine.jfif"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9974988c-7b9a-11f1-9a4c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Jin-Type-094-Class-Ballistic-Missile-Submarine.jfif" type="" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c5720654-7b9a-11f1-85a0-5b9af79f737d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 08:05:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Experts to deliver verdict on EU social media controls for children</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260713-experts-to-deliver-verdict-on-eu-social-media-controls-for-children</link><description>
An expert committee is due to deliver its recommendations on Monday on how the European Union should regulate children's access to social media, including a potential blanket ban. More than 20 countries worldwide, including France, have already implemented or proposed age restrictions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b8b57e38-f9ee-11f0-b804-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-82KW3GN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b8b57e38-f9ee-11f0-b804-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-82KW3GN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f4d90148-7dd6-11f1-a90a-4126f2da51c4</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 05:35:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b8b57e38-f9ee-11f0-b804-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-82KW3GN.jpg">© AFP - DAVID GRAY </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>China's rising foie gras industry has France looking over its shoulder</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260712-china-s-rising-foie-gras-industry-has-france-looking-over-its-shoulder</link><description>
China has risen rapidly to become the world's second-largest producer of foie gras, but producers in France say they are not yet worried about losing their long-held dominance of one of the country's best-known delicacies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6a231470-7166-11f1-a633-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-20T001111Z-1347002243-RC26YKAZ0BQ4-RTRMADP-3-CHINA-FRANCE-FOIE-GRAS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6a231470-7166-11f1-a633-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-20T001111Z-1347002243-RC26YKAZ0BQ4-RTRMADP-3-CHINA-FRANCE-FOIE-GRAS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4e11bada-7160-11f1-80ca-c19e380bf25d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 09:53:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6a231470-7166-11f1-a633-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-20T001111Z-1347002243-RC26YKAZ0BQ4-RTRMADP-3-CHINA-FRANCE-FOIE-GRAS.jpg">© Reuters/Tingshu Wang</source><dc:creator>Zeenat Hansrod</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>As Germany cuts a deal on US missiles, Europe weighs up dependence on Washington</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260712-as-germany-cuts-a-deal-on-us-missiles-europe-weighs-up-dependence-on-washington-tomahawk</link><description>
Germany is set to buy Tomahawk missiles to plug an urgent gap in its defence, in spite of a European Union drive to lessen dependence on American weapon systems. The deal comes after a Franco-German tank maker's stock market listing stalled and a flagship European fighter jet project collapsed. Can Europe really arm itself, or is autonomy a pipe dream?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d35edad0-9d38-11f0-b06f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36PY84L.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d35edad0-9d38-11f0-b06f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36PY84L.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7885640c-7c1d-11f1-aa2b-63849889c913</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 07:04:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d35edad0-9d38-11f0-b06f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36PY84L.jpg">©  AUSTRALIAN DEFENCE / AFP</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>What makes the Sultanate of Oman the Gulf's geopolitical exception?</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260711-what-makes-the-sultanate-of-oman-the-gulf-s-geopolitical-exception</link><description>
Removed from the theatrics of petrodollar politics seen across the rest of the Gulf, the Sultanate of Oman's famed discretion and diplomacy have made it an indispensable intermediary in the region.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8bda129e-73c3-11f1-9d8d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26180378011196.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8bda129e-73c3-11f1-9d8d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26180378011196.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3e36a894-79ff-11f1-a428-193d4865c5be</guid><pubDate>Sat, 11 Jul 2026 15:15:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8bda129e-73c3-11f1-9d8d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26180378011196.jpg">© AP Photo/Michel Euler</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Capital punishment in Pakistan: 'Islam does not promote the death penalty'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260711-capital-punishment-in-pakistan-islam-does-not-promote-the-death-penalty</link><description>
Around the world, a total of 47 countries still retain capital punishment – including Pakistan. Barrister Sarah Belal founded the Justice Project Pakistan in 2009 to represent the most vulnerable Pakistani prisoners facing the death penalty, at home and abroad. RFI met her in Paris.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8c0ebb4c-7bbc-11f1-8b9e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Justice-Project-Pakistan-rally.jfif"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8c0ebb4c-7bbc-11f1-8b9e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Justice-Project-Pakistan-rally.jfif" type="" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3f1027a6-7bba-11f1-b8ea-9747d6d62468</guid><pubDate>Sat, 11 Jul 2026 10:57:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8c0ebb4c-7bbc-11f1-8b9e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Justice-Project-Pakistan-rally.jfif">© JPP</source><dc:creator>Zeenat Hansrod</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Iran strikes Gulf neighbours after new US attacks</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260711-iran-strikes-gulf-neighbours-after-new-us-attacks</link><description>
Tehran announced it was closing the Strait of Hormuz on Sunday and launched missiles and drones at its Gulf neighbours, in retaliation for new US strikes following an attack by Iranian forces on a merchant vessel that was abandoned in flames by its crew.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/05400d62-74f7-11f1-bafd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/e7c23327786f81add837233b161f4dbce07d6ccb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/05400d62-74f7-11f1-bafd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/e7c23327786f81add837233b161f4dbce07d6ccb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dccc9e2e-7d0f-11f1-9958-51c68aff20dd</guid><pubDate>Sat, 11 Jul 2026 10:04:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/05400d62-74f7-11f1-bafd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/e7c23327786f81add837233b161f4dbce07d6ccb.jpg">© - / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>EU lawmakers give digital euro the green light, but rollout still years away</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260710-eu-lawmakers-give-digital-euro-the-green-light-but-rollout-still-years-away</link><description>
EU lawmakers on Thursday backed kickstarting negotiations on creating a digital version of the euro, as the European Union races to introduce the currency. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81fe24b6-7b9f-11f1-8af5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-96UV6ZR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81fe24b6-7b9f-11f1-8af5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-96UV6ZR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d0862a66-7b9f-11f1-92d7-5b9af79f737d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 10 Jul 2026 19:40:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81fe24b6-7b9f-11f1-8af5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-96UV6ZR.jpg">AFP - NICOLAS TUCAT</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Israel's recognition of the Armenian genocide unsettles Turkey and Azerbaijan</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260710-israel-s-recognition-of-the-armenian-genocide-unsettles-turkey-and-azerbaijan</link><description>
Israel's parliament voted on 29 June 2026 to recognise the 1915 Armenian genocide, breaking with decades of official reticence on the issue. RFI spoke to three regional experts to unpack the politics behind the vote and its fallout: Gerald Steinberg, professor at Bar-Ilan University in Tel Aviv; Richard Giragossian, director of the Regional Studies Centre in Yerevan; and Ilter Turan, professor at Bilgi University in Istanbul.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/19b61174-755b-11f1-8c19-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP19303447525609.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/19b61174-755b-11f1-8c19-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP19303447525609.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3bd08e7a-79f1-11f1-bf35-efc684573f63</guid><pubDate>Fri, 10 Jul 2026 12:00:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Trump says US will give Ukraine licence to build Patriot missiles</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260709-trump-at-nato-summit-says-us-will-let-ukraine-build-patriot-missiles</link><description>
The United States will grant Ukraine a licence to manufacture Patriot missile interceptors domestically, President Donald Trump announced from this week's NATO summit – as Kyiv's stockpile of the US-made air defence system runs critically low amid intensifying Russian strikes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/95cf88de-7af2-11f1-b1b0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-24T104043Z-945930775-RC2VIIAAQ0GA-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-TRUMP-MUNITIONS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/95cf88de-7af2-11f1-b1b0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-24T104043Z-945930775-RC2VIIAAQ0GA-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-TRUMP-MUNITIONS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bf49f3f2-7b74-11f1-b8f7-b9ff6fe6370e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 09 Jul 2026 14:27:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/95cf88de-7af2-11f1-b1b0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-24T104043Z-945930775-RC2VIIAAQ0GA-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-TRUMP-MUNITIONS.jpg">© Jacek Marczewski/Agencja Wyborcz/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>UK to lead European initiative to fund next generation of long-range missiles</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260709-uk-to-lead-european-initiative-to-fund-next-generation-of-long-range-missiles</link><description>
The United Kingdom, France, Germany and other European countries will spend more than $50 billion over the next 10 years to develop long-range precision weapons in a boost to NATO's defence capabilities, the UK government announced on Wednesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/999ef8aa-7acf-11f1-93dd-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-43CC72H.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/999ef8aa-7acf-11f1-93dd-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-43CC72H.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f567bc30-7acf-11f1-a6ea-9188a17f314e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 09 Jul 2026 10:12:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/999ef8aa-7acf-11f1-93dd-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-43CC72H.jpg">AFP - RICHARD POHLE</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Western Europe records hottest ever June as climate change drives heatwaves</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260709-western-europe-records-hottest-ever-june-as-climate-change-drives-heatwaves</link><description>
Western Europe experienced its warmest June on record, as a heatwave at the end of the month in many countries broke temperature records. The confirmation from the European Union’s climate monitor comes as many countries are facing a third heatwave this week since May.
